Upstream-Status: Pending
Exit: Drop when freedesktop-sdk resolves setuptools-scm git-describe timeouts at the fdsdk level (e.g. by actually staging tag refs into the sandbox).
Subject: python3-setuptools-scm: bypass git-describe with SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION

The ref-format: git-describe patch (0004) was insufficient. Observation
from build r9wtl: patch 0004 was applied (log confirms git apply
succeeded for 0004 and 0005), but setuptools-scm still failed with the
same subprocess.TimeoutExpired at the same action hash (5a3c6508) as
the pre-patch run. ref-format changes how the ref is serialized in the
element YAML but does not push tag refs into the staged sandbox, so
git describe --match 'setuptools-scm-*' still has nothing to match
and exhausts the 40s subprocess timeout.

Setting SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION_FOR_SETUPTOOLS_SCM in the
element's build env instructs setuptools-scm to use the given string
verbatim as the package version and skip VCS detection entirely. This
is the upstream-documented escape hatch for hermetic/sandboxed builds.
Version picked to match the element's existing ref
(setuptools-scm-v10.3.4-0-gb27f5973...).

Resolves: setuptools-scm#957 (upstream-documented workaround).

diff --git a/elements/components/python3-setuptools-scm.bst b/elements/components/python3-setuptools-scm.bst
--- a/elements/components/python3-setuptools-scm.bst
+++ b/elements/components/python3-setuptools-scm.bst
@@ -18,6 +18,10 @@ runtime-depends:
 variables:
   command-subdir: setuptools-scm

+environment:
+  # setuptools-scm#957 workaround: skip git-describe (times out in sandbox).
+  SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION_FOR_SETUPTOOLS_SCM: "10.3.4"
+
 sources:
 - kind: git_repo
   url: github:pypa/setuptools_scm.git
